V100 (192.168.7.3) MTP speculative decoding, 2026-09-26
repo: ~/llama-cpp-sm70 @ 793dc79a2
model: Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-HauhauCS-Aggressive-IQ4_XS.gguf
env: GGML_V100_FA=0, llama-server -ngl 99 -c 8192 -b 2048 -ub 2048
request: temperature 0, seed 7, cache_prompt false, prose prompt, n_predict 400

================================================================
The model ships its own MTP head
================================================================
GGUF metadata: qwen35.nextn_predict_layers = 1

llama.cpp exposes this as --spec-type draft-mtp. No second model file is needed:
the server log says "creating MTP draft context against the target model", and it
costs 552 MiB of extra VRAM instead of a whole second model.

  --- base
    tg=37.03 tok/s
  --- mtp  (--spec-type draft-mtp)
    tg=53.44 tok/s   acceptance 54.8% (247 accepted / 451 drafted), mean len 2.64
    (+44.3%)

Compare with an external draft model (Qwen3.5-2B Q8, --spec-type draft-simple):
acceptance 24.3% on the same prompt and 16.51 tok/s, i.e. -55.4%. An MTP head
trained against the target's own distribution is the difference between +44% and
-55%.

n-gram self-speculation (--spec-type ngram-mod / ngram-cache) did not engage at
all: no draft_n in the response, throughput identical to baseline.

================================================================
Draft depth: the default is already optimal
================================================================
--spec-draft-n-max sweep, same prose prompt, temp 0:

| n_max        | tg tok/s | acceptance | text vs baseline |
|--------------|---------:|-----------:|------------------|
| default (3)  |    53.44 |      54.8% | (not hashed)     |
| 4            |    51.31 |      44.8% | IDENTICAL        |
| 8            |    30.47 |      23.8% | **DIFFERS**      |
| 16           |    23.15 |      12.8% | IDENTICAL        |
| adaptive(8)  |    52.29 |      54.8% | IDENTICAL        |

Acceptance decays fast with depth, so drafting deeper than ~3 is pure loss. Do not
raise --spec-draft-n-max.

================================================================
Caveat: one depth changed the output
================================================================
Speculative decoding must be lossless at temperature 0, and n_max 4 / 16 /
adaptive all produced byte-identical text. n_max=8 did not (sha f490399dc8e5 vs
2e8a2141da13).

Most likely cause: the verify step batches n_max+1 tokens, which changes the GEMM
shape and therefore the accumulation order, so logits shift slightly and an argmax
near a tie can flip. That matches the pattern - shallower and deeper depths
matched, one in the middle did not.

This is a numerics caveat, not a proof of a bug, but it means "speculation is
lossless" should not be assumed without a per-config text check. At the
recommended default depth the text is identical.

